**Key observations:**
- **Best single measurement:** 17.5wt, 25°C mixing, 5°C bath, 12mm/s, N₂, 550s wait, 1450s nips → 778 MPa (run1), but run2 gave only 342 MPa with high CV (0.25). These two runs are highly discrepant — the candidate is NOT confirmed.
- **Second best:** 17.5wt, 65°C, 10°C bath, 6mm/s, N₂, 15s, 1800s → run1: 709 MPa, run2: 475 MPa. Also discrepant between runs.
- **Third best:** 17.5wt, 50°C, 20°C bath, 7mm/s, N₂, 90s, 1250s → 683 MPa (single measurement, no repeat).
- **Fourth best:** 18.5wt, 25°C, 5°C bath, 19mm/s, no N₂, 330s, 1800s → 667 MPa (single measurement, no repeat).

**Validation status:**
- The 778 MPa candidate (17.5wt, 25°C, 5°C, 12mm/s, N₂, 550s, 1450s) has been repeated twice. Run1=778, Run2=342. These are dramatically different — high variability, not confirmed. The mean of the two runs is ~560 MPa, not exceptional.
- The 709 MPa candidate (17.5wt, 65°C, 10°C, 6mm/s, N₂, 15s, 1800s) has run1=709, run2=475. Mean ~592 MPa, also variable.
- The 683 MPa candidate (17.5wt, 50°C, 20°C, 7mm/s, N₂, 90s, 1250s) has only one measurement.
- The 667 MPa candidate (18.5wt, 25°C, 5°C, 19mm/s, no N₂, 330s, 1800s) has only one measurement.

**Mode: Explore.** The instruction is to prioritize design-space coverage and novelty. With 33 experiments done, the space is reasonably sampled but there are still sparse regions. Looking at the diversity context:
- `bath_temp` has only 5 unique values (5, 10, 15, 20, 25°C) — all covered
- `polymer_wt` has 9 unique values from 17–21 — sparse around 17.5–18 at certain bath/mixing combos
- `mixing_temp` has 12 unique values — fairly well covered
- `nips_bath_wait_time` has 13 unique values — moderate coverage

**Sparse regions to explore:**
- High mixing_temp (70-80°C) + intermediate bath_temp (10-15°C) + higher polymer_wt (19-20wt) + moderate-high pullcast speed + N₂ + intermediate wait time — this combination is underrepresented.
- Specifically: mixing_temp=75°C, bath_temp=15°C, polymer_wt=20wt, pullcast_speed=19mm/s, N₂=True, wait=400s, nips=1600s — this is far from existing points.

